      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-184231",
      ":question/problem": "Prove that if $n$ is odd, then $3n+5$ is even.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=\\,${{field-1}} for {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & ={{field-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-4}}. Since $a$ is {{field-5}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-6}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n+5 & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n+5$ is {{field-8}}."
    },
